# Environment

- Live cPanel PHP is **7.4.33**. CMS PHP must parse on 7.4. Do not use PHP 8-only syntax in `cms/`.
- Live MySQL is **localhost on the server** (`thegameh_tgh_cms`). Windows cannot open remote 3306. Local CMS uses gitignored `cms/config.local.php` (JSON/dev).
- Local ops/booking: `npm run local` (PHP `:8765` + Vite `:5173`). Ops: http://localhost:5173/ops/login. CMS admin: http://localhost:5173/admin/login.php (Vite proxies `/admin` to PHP). Sign in with `devadmin` / `dev123`. Dummy seed is `cms/data/ops-dummy.json`; writable copy is gitignored `cms/dev-data/bookings.json`. Do not use live `/ops` for UI iteration. `npm run dev` alone has no PHP — `/admin` is then a React 404.
- Deploy is GitHub `main` → FTPS (`.github/workflows/deploy-ftp.yml`). Protect `cms/config.php` and uploads from overwrite.
- Never commit `cms/config.local.php`, `.env`, passwords, bcrypt hashes, or PII SQL under `cms/dev-data/`.
- Public Book CTAs stay on same-origin `/book` (type chooser). Corporate service CTAs may use `/book?category=corporate`. Keep `/book/social` and `/book/corporate` as redirects. Do not point CTAs back at Bubble.
- On `/book` (and old `/book/social` `/book/corporate` redirects), do not render floating WhatsApp/Call FABs. They overlay age/date/time menus and **Submit booking** (`fixed z-40`). Booking Submit must stay a real `<button type="submit">` (not clay `Button` with `disabled:pointer-events-none`). Do not wrap that CTA in `overflow-x-clip`. Save `event_category` as `social` or `corporate` from the type step.
- Ops is `noindex`. `robots.txt` disallows `/ops`, `/admin`, `/cms`.
- Ops SPA must redirect to `/ops/login` when the session is gone (poll `me.php`; `401`/`419` on events APIs). Do not leave a logged-out workspace on screen.
- Event status ENUM is `pending`/`cancelled`/`completed`. `cms_ops_migrate_cancelled_status()` maps leftover `upcoming` rows. Do not reintroduce `upcoming`.
- Booking alerts use free **Resend** (`POST https://api.resend.com/emails`). Put `mail.resend_api_key` only in `cms/config.php` / `config.local.php` (never git). Recipient is CMS **Booking alerts** (`settings.php`), default `thegamehourr@gmail.com`. Mail failure must not fail the booking save. `from` stays `onboarding@resend.dev` until a domain is verified in Resend.
- Booking alerts fire only after the payment screenshot is saved. Body matches the Vijay booking copy (date, venue, time, participants, requirements, Insta, client). Screenshot is attached. Optional `mail.resend_template_id` uses the same free quota; Resend template variable values max 2000 chars. A send-only API key cannot GET/create templates; sending with `template.id` still works. Live `cms/config.php` needs the same template id by hand.
- Windows PHP curl needs a CA bundle (`curl.cainfo` / `extras/ssl/cacert.pem`). Without it, test email is SSL errno 60 (“Could not reach Resend”). Do not disable CURLOPT_SSL_VERIFYPEER.
